# Environment Guide — {{project_slug}}

Use this guide for sandbox and production configuration. Do not commit real secrets.

## Sandbox defaults

| Variable | Sandbox value | Source |
|---|---|---|
| `APP_NAME` | `{{project_name}}` | project name |
| `APP_ENV` | `local` | sandbox |
| `APP_DEBUG` | `true` | sandbox |
| `APP_URL` | read from `docs/larv/07-runtime/sandbox-url.txt` | bootstrap |
| `DB_CONNECTION` | `pgsql` | bootstrap |
| `DB_HOST` | `127.0.0.1` | bootstrap |
| `DB_PORT` | `5432` | bootstrap |
| `DB_DATABASE` | `larv_{{project_slug}}` with dashes converted to underscores | bootstrap |
| `DB_USERNAME` | `larv` unless overridden | bootstrap |
| `DB_PASSWORD` | `larv` unless overridden | bootstrap |
| `CACHE_STORE` | `database` or plan-specific value | app plan |
| `QUEUE_CONNECTION` | `database`, `redis`, or plan-specific value | app plan |
| `SESSION_DRIVER` | `database` or plan-specific value | app plan |
| `MAIL_MAILER` | provider-specific | user |
| `MAIL_HOST` | provider-specific | user |
| `MAIL_PORT` | provider-specific | user |
| `MAIL_USERNAME` | provider-specific secret | user |
| `MAIL_PASSWORD` | provider-specific secret | user |
| `MAIL_FROM_ADDRESS` | verified sender | user |

## Production values to collect

Ask the user or read from Laravel Cloud:

```dotenv
APP_NAME="{{project_name}}"
APP_ENV=production
APP_KEY=<generate with php artisan key:generate --show>
APP_DEBUG=false
APP_URL=https://<production-domain>
DB_CONNECTION=pgsql
DB_HOST=<laravel-cloud-db-host>
DB_PORT=5432
DB_DATABASE=<laravel-cloud-db-name>
DB_USERNAME=<laravel-cloud-db-user>
DB_PASSWORD=<laravel-cloud-db-password>

CACHE_STORE=<database|redis>
QUEUE_CONNECTION=<database|redis>
SESSION_DRIVER=<database|redis>

MAIL_MAILER=<smtp|resend|postmark|mailgun|ses>
MAIL_HOST=<mail-host>
MAIL_PORT=<mail-port>
MAIL_USERNAME=<mail-username>
MAIL_PASSWORD=<mail-password>
MAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=<verified-sender>
MAIL_FROM_NAME="{{project_name}}"
```

## Test credentials

Sandbox review uses normal login with seeded test credentials. Document each seeded user's email/username and password, role, permissions scope, and recommended test flow in `docs/user-manual/seed-data.md`.

Do not add a navbar impersonation/user-switching UI unless the product requirements explicitly ask for one.

## Package-specific values

Only collect values for packages selected in `docs/larv/03-design/package-decisions.md`.

### Cashier / payments

Stripe:

```dotenv
STRIPE_KEY=<stripe-publishable-key>
STRIPE_SECRET=<stripe-secret-key>
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=<stripe-webhook-signing-secret>
CASHIER_CURRENCY=usd
```

Paddle:

```dotenv
PADDLE_CLIENT_SIDE_TOKEN=<paddle-client-side-token>
PADDLE_API_KEY=<paddle-api-key>
PADDLE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=<paddle-webhook-secret>
```

### Reverb / realtime

```dotenv
REVERB_APP_ID=<reverb-app-id>
REVERB_APP_KEY=<reverb-app-key>
REVERB_APP_SECRET=<reverb-app-secret>
REVERB_HOST=<reverb-host>
REVERB_PORT=443
REVERB_SCHEME=https
```

### Scout / search

Meilisearch:

```dotenv
SCOUT_DRIVER=meilisearch
MEILISEARCH_HOST=<meilisearch-host>
MEILISEARCH_KEY=<meilisearch-key>
```

Typesense:

```dotenv
SCOUT_DRIVER=typesense
TYPESENSE_HOST=<typesense-host>
TYPESENSE_API_KEY=<typesense-api-key>
```

### Filesystem / uploads

S3-compatible storage:

```dotenv
FILESYSTEM_DISK=s3
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<access-key>
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=<secret-key>
AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=<region>
AWS_BUCKET=<bucket-name>
AWS_URL=<optional-public-url>
```

### Socialite / OAuth

Repeat per provider selected by the app plan:

```dotenv
<PROVIDER>_CLIENT_ID=<oauth-client-id>
<PROVIDER>_CLIENT_SECRET=<oauth-client-secret>
<PROVIDER>_REDIRECT_URI=https://<production-domain>/auth/<provider>/callback
```

### Horizon / Redis queues

```dotenv
QUEUE_CONNECTION=redis
REDIS_HOST=<redis-host>
REDIS_PASSWORD=<redis-password-or-null>
REDIS_PORT=6379
```

### Octane

Use only when the deploy target supports long-running PHP workers:

```dotenv
OCTANE_SERVER=<frankenphp|swoole|roadrunner>
```

## Secret handling

- Put production secrets only in Laravel Cloud environment variables or the selected secret manager.
- Do not paste production secrets into `docs/`.
- If a secret is accidentally committed, rotate it immediately.
